  "title": "tribus Suburana (Succusana)",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/people"
  ],
  "details": "<p>Under the reign of Servius Tullius, the people of Rome were divided into four large urban tribes (<em>Collina</em>, <em>Esquilina</em>, <em>Palatina</em>, and <em>Suburana</em>), which corresponded to the four urban regions that Servius created.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The tribus Suburana (also called Succusana) was an urban tribe of Rome, reportedly established by Servius Tullius.",
